Why they differ. A specification whose reader may not keep a copy after
thirty-two days cannot be cited, and the argument this work rests on is that
somebody can implement the format from the specification alone. Implementing
a format from its specification is not modifying the specification's text, so
the prose can be kept and cited, and the format implemented from it, while
there remains one text of what the format is. The evidence is there to be
checked, and checking it often means publishing a changed copy of it.

